{"name":"Wooden Wagon","hex":"#815a48","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wooden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of wood.","As if made of wood; moving awkwardly, or speaking with dull lack of emotion."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wooden"},{"term":"wagon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A heavier four-wheeled (normally horse-drawn) vehicle designed to carry goods (or sometimes people). .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Abbreviation of toy wagon; A child's riding toy, with the same structure as a wagon (sense 1), pulled or steered by a long handle attached to the front."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To load into a wagon in preparation for transportation; to transport by means of a wagon.","To travel in a wagon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wagon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wood","blocks":[{"text":"Wood is a structural tissue/material found as xylem in the stems and roots of trees and other woody plants. Being a natural material, it is characterized as an organic material – a natural composite of cellulosic fibers that are strong in tension and embedded in a matrix of lignin and hemicelluloses that resists compression."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/16_wood_samples.jpg/330px-16_wood_samples.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wood"},{"title":"Wagon","blocks":[{"text":"A wagon is a heavy four-wheeled vehicle pulled by draft animals or on occasion by humans, used for transporting goods, commodities, agricultural materials, supplies and sometimes people."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Wagon_Ride_P9190071.jpg/330px-Wagon_Ride_P9190071.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wagon"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia